		{
			"to": "blood/stained-film",
			"why": "Paul Ehrlich, who sorted blood cells by the aniline dyes they took, sat in the audience when Koch showed the tubercle bacillus made visible by an aniline stain in 1882."
		},
		{
			"to": "food/pasteurization",
			"why": "In 1901 Koch said the cattle tubercle bacillus so seldom infected people that nothing need be done about milk; the evidence that it did was the strongest argument for pasteurizing it."
		},
		{
			"to": "food/potato-blight",
			"why": "De Bary proved by infection experiments that a fungus caused potato blight decades before Koch set out how to prove that a microbe causes a disease."
		}
